[service icons]    ← parent = Subnet id\n │       ├─ [Security Group]           ← parent = VPC id  (NO edges)\n │       ├─ [Monitoring Group]         ← parent = VPC id  (NO edges)\n │       ├─ [Integration Group]        ← parent = VPC id  (NO edges)\n │       └─ [Management Group]         ← parent = VPC id  (NO edges)\n └─ [Edge/Global Layer]                ← parent = Cloud id (sibling of Region, still INSIDE Cloud)\n     └─ DNS / CDN / WAF / static       ← parent = Edge layer id\n```\n\n**Outer-layer wrap rules:**\n1. Create the Cloud boundary first. Its `parent="1"`. Size it large enough to contain Region + Edge + padding.\n2. Region is **inside** Cloud (`parent=<cloud-id>`). VPC is **inside** Region. Zones/subnets/groups are **inside** VPC. Services are **inside** their subnet or supporting group.\n3. **FORBIDDEN:** Region, VPC, Zone, Subnet, Security/Monitoring/Integration/Management, or Edge as `parent="1"` siblings floating beside the Cloud box. If it belongs in the hierarchy, it must be a child of the layer above it.\n4. **FORBIDDEN:** placing an inner box with absolute canvas coordinates while `parent="1"` so it only overlaps the outer box visually. Overlap ≠ containment.\n5. Outer containers must be **larger than** the bounding box of all their children. Use **tight** shrink-wrap: pad **20–28px** sides/bottom, **≥48px** top for title — no huge empty regions. Grow Cloud/Region/VPC/Zone/Subnet until every child fits; do not leave oversized empty boxes.\n6. Optional **Users / Internet / Client** icons may sit outside Cloud on `parent="1"` (left of Cloud). Everything else cloud-related stays wrapped inside Cloud.\n\n## Leaf Footprint — UNDER-ICON LABELS (CRITICAL)\n\nService leaves use `verticalLabelPosition=bottom` — the **label draws below** the icon box. Parent sizing must account for that extra band, not only the 78×78 icon geometry.\n\n- Visual footprint height ≈ `icon.height + ~28` (label band) when `verticalLabelPosition=bottom`\n- Parent must contain: `